From 1df2cd490ebe3c9721dbce3f3c6d0b922540e40c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitry B <dimitryB@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:35:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 29/30] types: error codes for the exact bip122 scheme
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The exact scheme on bip122 (BTC paid on Bitcoin L1, checked through
Hemi's hBK) reports its failures with codes shaped like x402 v2 §9's
exact EVM ones:

- invalid_exact_bip122_payload_transaction_not_found: the transaction is
  not known to the facilitator's view of Bitcoin
- invalid_exact_bip122_payload_vout: it has no output at the payload's vout
- invalid_exact_bip122_payload_recipient_mismatch: the output does not pay
  the address derived for the payment
- invalid_exact_bip122_payload_value_mismatch: the output is worth less
  than the amount
- invalid_exact_bip122_payload_unconfirmed: too few confirmations
- invalid_exact_bip122_pay_to: payTo is not an extended public key for
  the network

Each has a PaymentVerificationError variant that carries its message. A
generic InvalidPaymentRequirements(String) reports requirements a scheme
cannot use (an asset, flow or extra field it does not take) as §9
invalid_payment_requirements; until now only AcceptedRequirementsMismatch
could, with a fixed message.

All are verdicts on a payment that could be read, so handlers.rs answers
them with 200 like every other rejection; its status test lists them.
Existing variants and their serialization are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/x402-facilitator-local/src/handlers.rs |   8 ++
 crates/x402-types/src/proto/mod.rs            | 134 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 142 insertions(+)

